#: src/ai/external-agents.md:1
msgid "External Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:3
msgid ""
"Zed supports many external agents, including CLI-based ones, through the "
"[Agent Client Protocol (ACP)](https://agentclientprotocol.com)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed supports [Gemini CLI](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli) (the "
"reference ACP implementation), [Claude Code](https://www.anthropic.com/"
"claude-code), [Codex](https://developers.openai.com/codex), [GitHub Copilot]"
"(https://github.com/github/copilot-language-server-release), and [additional "
"agents](#add-more-agents) you can configure."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:7
msgid ""
"Note that Zed's interaction with external agents is strictly UI-based; the "
"billing, legal, and terms arrangement is directly between you and the agent "
"provider. Zed does not charge for use of external agents, and our [zero-data "
"retention agreements/privacy guarantees](./ai-improvement.md) are **_only_** "
"applicable for Zed's hosted models."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:10
msgid "Gemini CLI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:12
msgid ""
"Zed provides the ability to run [Gemini CLI](https://github.com/google-"
"gemini/gemini-cli) directly in the [agent panel](./agent-panel.md). Under "
"the hood we run Gemini CLI in the background, and talk to it over ACP."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:15 src/ai/external-agents.md:76
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:145
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:17
msgid ""
"First open the agent panel with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-?|ctrl-?</"
"kbd>, and then use the `+` button in the top right to start a new Gemini CLI "
"thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:19 src/ai/external-agents.md:80
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:150
msgid ""
"If you'd like to bind this to a keyboard shortcut, you can do so by editing "
"your `keymap.json` file via the `zed: open keymap file` command to include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:24 src/ai/external-agents.md:85
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:155
msgid "\"bindings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:25
msgid "\"cmd-alt-g\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:25 src/ai/external-agents.md:86
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:156
msgid "\"agent::NewExternalAgentThread\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:25 src/ai/external-agents.md:86
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:156
msgid "\"agent\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:25 src/ai/external-agents.md:42
msgid "\"gemini\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:31 src/ai/external-agents.md:100
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:178
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:33
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Gemini CLI thread, Zed will install [@google/"
"gemini-cli](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli). This installation "
"is only available to Zed and is kept up to date as you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:36
msgid ""
"By default, Zed will use this managed version of Gemini CLI even if you have "
"it installed globally. However, you can configure it to use a version in "
"your `PATH` by adding this to your settings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:41 src/ai/external-agents.md:111
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:232
msgid "\"agent_servers\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:43
msgid "\"ignore_system_version\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:49 src/ai/external-agents.md:92
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:162
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:51
msgid ""
"After you have Gemini CLI running, you'll be prompted to choose your "
"authentication method."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:53
msgid ""
"Most users should click the \"Log in with Google\". This will cause a "
"browser window to pop-up and auth directly with Gemini CLI. Zed does not see "
"your OAuth or access tokens in this case."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:57
msgid ""
"You can also use the \"Gemini API Key\". If you select this, and have the "
"`GEMINI_API_KEY` set, then we will use that. Otherwise Zed will prompt you "
"for an API key which will be stored securely in your keychain, and used to "
"start Gemini CLI from within Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:61
msgid ""
"The \"Vertex AI\" option is for those who are using [Vertex AI](https://"
"cloud.google.com/vertex-ai), and have already configured their environment "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:63
msgid ""
"For more information, see the [Gemini CLI docs](https://github.com/google-"
"gemini/gemini-cli/blob/main/docs/index.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:65 src/ai/external-agents.md:121
#: src/ai/external-agents.md:185
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:67
msgid ""
"Gemini CLI supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent: code "
"generation, refactoring, debugging, and Q&A. Add context by @-mentioning "
"files, recent threads, or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:69
msgid ""
"Some agent panel features are not yet available with Gemini CLI: editing "
"past messages, resuming threads from history, and checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:71
msgid "Claude Code"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:73
msgid ""
"Similar to Gemini CLI, you can also run [Claude Code](https://www.anthropic."
"com/claude-code) directly via Zed's [agent panel](./agent-panel.md). Under "
"the hood, Zed runs Claude Code and communicate to it over ACP, through [a "
"dedicated adapter](https://github.com/zed-industries/claude-code-acp)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:78
msgid ""
"Open the agent panel with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-?|ctrl-?</kbd>, and "
"then use the `+` button in the top right to start a new Claude Code thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:86 src/ai/external-agents.md:156
msgid "\"cmd-alt-c\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:86
msgid "\"claude_code\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:94
msgid ""
"As of version `0.202.7`, authentication to Zed's Claude Code installation is "
"decoupled entirely from Zed's agent. That is to say, an Anthropic API key "
"added via the [Zed Agent's settings](./llm-providers.md#anthropic) will "
"_not_ be utilized by Claude Code for authentication and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:97
msgid ""
"To ensure you're using your billing method of choice, [open a new Claude "
"Code thread](./agent-panel.md#new-thread). Then, run `/login`, and "
"authenticate either via API key, or via `Log in with Claude Code` to use a "
"Claude Pro/Max subscription."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:102
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Claude Code thread, Zed will install [@zed-"
"industries/claude-code-acp](https://github.com/zed-industries/claude-code-"
"acp). This installation is only available to Zed and is kept up to date as "
"you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:105
msgid ""
"Zed will always use this managed version of the Claude Code adapter, which "
"includes a vendored version of the Claude Code CLI, even if you have it "
"installed globally."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:107
msgid ""
"If you want to override the executable used by the adapter, you can set the "
"`CLAUDE_CODE_EXECUTABLE` environment variable in your settings to the path "
"of your preferred executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:112
msgid "\"claude\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:113 src/ai/external-agents.md:237
msgid "\"env\""
msgstr "\"env\""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:114
msgid "\"CLAUDE_CODE_EXECUTABLE\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:114
msgid "\"/path/to/alternate-claude-code-executable\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:123
msgid ""
"Claude Code supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent. Add "
"context by @-mentioning files, recent threads, diagnostics, or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:125
msgid ""
"In complement to talking to it [over ACP](https://agentclientprotocol.com), "
"Zed relies on the [Claude Code SDK](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/"
"claude-code/sdk/sdk-overview) to support some of its specific features. "
"However, the SDK doesn't yet expose everything needed to fully support all "
"of them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:128
msgid ""
"Slash Commands: A subset of [built-in commands](https://docs.anthropic.com/"
"en/docs/claude-code/slash-commands#built-in-slash-commands) are supported, "
"while [custom slash commands](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/"
"slash-commands#custom-slash-commands) are fully supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:129
msgid ""
"[Subagents](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/sub-agents) are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:130
msgid ""
"[Hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide) are "
"currently _not_ supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:132
msgid ""
"Some [agent panel](./agent-panel.md) features are not yet available with "
"Claude Code: editing past messages, resuming threads from history, and "
"checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:134
msgid "CLAUDE.md"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:136
msgid ""
"Claude Code in Zed will automatically use any `CLAUDE.md` file found in your "
"project root, project subdirectories, or root `.claude` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:138
msgid ""
"If you don't have a `CLAUDE.md` file, you can ask Claude Code to create one "
"for you through the `init` slash command."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:140
msgid "Codex CLI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:142
msgid ""
"You can also run [Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex) directly via "
"Zed's [agent panel](./agent-panel.md). Under the hood, Zed runs Codex CLI "
"and communicates to it over ACP, through [a dedicated adapter](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/codex-acp)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:147
msgid ""
"As of version `0.208`, you should be able to use Codex directly from Zed. "
"Open the agent panel with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-?|ctrl-?</kbd>, and "
"then use the `+` button in the top right to start a new Codex thread."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:156
msgid "\"codex\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:164
msgid ""
"Authentication to Zed's Codex installation is decoupled entirely from Zed's "
"agent. That is to say, an OpenAI API key added via the [Zed Agent's settings]"
"(./llm-providers.md#openai) will _not_ be utilized by Codex for "
"authentication and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:167
msgid ""
"To ensure you're using your billing method of choice, [open a new Codex "
"thread](./agent-panel.md#new-thread). The first time you will be prompted to "
"authenticate with one of three methods:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:170
msgid ""
"Login with ChatGPT - allows you to use your existing, paid ChatGPT "
"subscription. _Note: This method isn't currently supported in remote "
"projects_"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:171
msgid ""
"`CODEX_API_KEY` - uses an API key you have set in your environment under the "
"variable `CODEX_API_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:172
msgid ""
"`OPENAI_API_KEY` - uses an API key you have set in your environment under "
"the variable `OPENAI_API_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:174
msgid ""
"If you are already logged in and want to change your authentication method, "
"type `/logout` in the thread and authenticate again."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:176
msgid ""
"If you want to use a third-party provider with Codex, you can configure that "
"with your [Codex config.toml](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/"
"config.md#model-selection) or pass extra [args/env variables](https://github."
"com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/config.md#model-selection) to your Codex "
"agent servers settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:180
msgid ""
"The first time you create a Codex thread, Zed will install [codex-acp]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/codex-acp). This installation is only "
"available to Zed and is kept up to date as you use the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:183
msgid ""
"Zed will always use this managed version of Codex even if you have it "
"installed globally."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:187
msgid ""
"Codex supports the same workflows as Zed's first-party agent. Add context by "
"@-mentioning files or symbols."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:189
msgid ""
"Some agent panel features are not yet available with Codex: editing past "
"messages, resuming threads from history, and checkpointing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:191
msgid "Add More Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:193
msgid "Via Agent Server Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:197
msgid ""
"Starting from `v0.221.x`, [the ACP Registry](https://agentclientprotocol.com/"
"registry) is the preferred way to install external agents in Zed. Learn more "
"about it in [the release blog post](https://zed.dev/blog/acp-registry). At "
"some point in the near future, Agent Server extensions will be deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:203
msgid ""
"Add more external agents to Zed by installing [Agent Server extensions](../"
"extensions/agent-servers.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:205
msgid ""
"See what agents are available by filtering for \"Agent Servers\" in the "
"extensions page, which you can access via the command palette with `zed: "
"extensions`, or the [Zed website](https://zed.dev/extensions?filter=agent-"
"servers)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:207
msgid "Via The ACP Registry"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:209
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:211
msgid ""
"As mentioned above, the Agent Server extensions will be deprecated in the "
"near future to give room to the ACP Registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:213
msgid ""
"[The ACP Registry](https://github.com/agentclientprotocol/registry) lets "
"developers distribute ACP-compatible agents to any client that implements "
"the protocol. Agents installed from the registry update automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:215
msgid ""
"At the moment, the registry is a curated set of agents, including only the "
"ones that [support authentication](https://agentclientprotocol.com/rfds/auth-"
"methods)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:217
msgid "Using it in Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:219
msgid ""
"Use the `zed: acp registry` command to quickly go to the ACP Registry page. "
"There's also a button (\"Add Agent\") that takes you there in the agent "
"panel's configuration view."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:222
msgid ""
"From there, you can click to install your preferred agent and it will become "
"available right away in the `+` icon button in the agent panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:224
msgid ""
"If you installed the same agent through both the extension and the registry, "
"the registry version takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:226
msgid "Custom Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:228
msgid ""
"You can also add agents through your `settings.json`, by specifying certain "
"fields under `agent_servers`, like so:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:233
msgid "\"My Custom Agent\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:234
msgid "\"type\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:234
msgid "\"custom\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:235
msgid "\"command\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:235
msgid "\"node\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:236
msgid "\"args\""
msgstr "\"args\""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:236
msgid "\"~/projects/agent/index.js\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:236
msgid "\"--acp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:243
msgid ""
"This can be useful if you're in the middle of developing a new agent that "
"speaks the protocol and you want to debug it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:245
msgid ""
"It's also possible to specify a custom path, arguments, or environment for "
"the builtin integrations by using the `claude` and `gemini` names."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:247
msgid "Debugging Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:249
msgid ""
"When using external agents in Zed, you can access the debug view via with "
"`dev: open acp logs` from the Command Palette. This lets you see the "
"messages being sent and received between Zed and the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:252
msgid "![The debug view for ACP logs.](https://zed.dev/img/acp/acp-logs.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:254
msgid ""
"It's helpful to attach data from this view if you're opening issues about "
"problems with external agents like Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:256
msgid "MCP Servers"
msgstr "MCP 伺服器"

#: src/ai/external-agents.md:258
msgid ""
"Note that for external agents, access to MCP servers [installed from Zed](./"
"mcp.md) may vary depending on the ACP implementation. For example, Claude "
"Code and Codex both support it, but Gemini CLI does not yet."
msgstr ""
